CI ownership and support
• The CI implementation is shared/owned by the EPI team. If a failure is caused by the shared CI process or shared template behavior, post the details in the EPI group chat.
• Include the pipeline name, run/build number, failing task name, error message, and whether the failure is reproducible.
• A frequent CI problem is a vulnerability/policy violation while creating the image (for example, a vulnerable language package or base-image component identified by JFrog Xray).
3. CD Template - azure-pipelines-cd.yaml
• The CD template receives the same five parameters and conditionally creates validation/deployment stages.
• Deployment jobs use the `EPE_AgentPool` with demands visible in the screenshots (`dynamic_agent_9` and `agent_env -equals prod`).
• Deployment jobs use `checkout: none`; the deployment work is performed through shell commands, secure files, registry operations, and gcloud commands rather than repository checkout.
Existing-image validation
• When `runBuild=false` and at least one deployment environment is selected, the template creates a `Validate_Image` stage.
• The validation job fails if `imageVersion` is still `NOT_REQUIRED`, with an error indicating that an existing image version is required when a new image is not being built.
• If a valid version is supplied, it is carried forward as the enterprise image tag for deployment.
Enterprise image tag resolution
• If `imageVersion` is supplied, the pipeline uses it directly as `EnterpriseImageTag`.
• If a new image was built, the pipeline calls the Azure DevOps Build Tags REST API using `System.AccessToken`.
• A small Python parser reads build tags and looks for `version=<value>` and `short_commit_id=<value>`; the resulting deployable image tag is formed as `version-short_commit_id`.
• If the expected build tags cannot be found, the pipeline logs a warning and sets a skip-deployment variable instead of attempting to deploy an unknown image.
• If no image version is provided while `runBuild=false`, the pipeline treats it as a hard configuration error.
