7. JFrog / Lucius and Vulnerability Troubleshooting
• The JFrog Platform screenshot shows Artifactory areas (Packages, Builds, Artifacts, Release Lifecycle) and Xray options including Scans List, Watch Violations, Reports, and On-Demand Scanning.
• When a CI image build fails because of a vulnerability or Xray policy violation, start by identifying the exact package/base-image component, severity/CVE, and the stage in which the policy blocked the build.
• For application dependency vulnerabilities, the typical fix is to move to an approved non-vulnerable dependency or base image, rebuild, and rerun the scan. Do not bypass an organizational security policy unless the approved exception process explicitly allows it.
• If the problem originates from the shared CI template, scanner configuration, or an enterprise-controlled base image, post the failure in the EPI group chat with the pipeline run and scan details.
