8. Common Failure Checks
Symptom
First checks
Existing image deployment fails immediately
Check `runBuild=false` and confirm `imageVersion` is not `NOT_REQUIRED`.
Deployment is skipped after a successful build
Inspect build tags. The YAML expects both `version=` and `short_commit_id=` values.
Secure file cannot be downloaded
Check Pipelines > Library > Secure files, file name, pipeline authorization, and permissions.
GCP authentication fails
Check the correct environment key, service-account permissions, key rotation/expiry/revocation, and target project.
GAR push/login fails
Check `gcloud auth configure-docker` / access-token login, registry hostname, DNS/HTTPS reachability, and IAM permissions.
Lucius/JFrog pull fails
Check the `lucius-config.json` secure file, Podman login, source image path/tag, and JFrog availability/policy.
Cloud Run revision is created but not Ready
Open Cloud Run revision logs and pipeline output; the YAML intentionally fails when latest-created != latest-ready.
UAT/PROD deployment is waiting
Check Azure DevOps Environment approvals/checks and confirm the required approver has acted.
CI build blocked by vulnerabilities
Review JFrog Xray scan/watch violation details; fix the vulnerable dependency/base image or contact EPI for shared-CI ownership issues.
